{"tool_name":"osprey_vis","contents":["oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"osprey_vis","home":"http://biodata.mshri.on.ca/osprey","summary":"Application for graphically representing physical and genetic biological interactions; is coupled with the General Repository of Interaction Datasets (The GRID); available for Unix and Windows.","addition_date":"2017-05-02T07:25:34Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:57Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:osprey_vis","credit":[{"email":"biogridadmin@gmail.com","name":"Biogrid Admin","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://osprey.thebiogrid.org/#documentation"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://osprey.thebiogrid.org/#tutorials"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Pathway or network prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3439"},{"term":"Pathway or network visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3083"},{"term":"Protein interaction network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0276"},{"term":"Protein interaction network comparison","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0277"}]}],"name":"The Osprey Network Visualization System","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"We have developed a software platform called Osprey for visualization and manipulation of complex interaction networks. Osprey builds data-rich graphical representations that are color-coded for gene function and experimental interaction data. Mouse-over functions allow rapid elaboration and organization of network diagrams in a spoke model format. User-defined large-scale datasets can be readily combined with Osprey for comparison of different methods.","authors":[{"name":"Breitkreutz B.J."},{"name":"Stark C."},{"name":"Tyers M."}],"citationCount":364,"date":"2003-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome biology